From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: camcc-sc8280xp: Vote MX for the PLLs

The camera PLLs run on the MX rail, at a level that grows with their
rate: SVS at 800 MHz, SVS_L1 at 1116 MHz (the PLL of a 558 MHz IFE), NOM
at 1520 MHz. The clock controller votes only MMCX, at LOW_SVS, so
nothing of the camera kept MX up; with the display on, it did. A 558 MHz
IFE with 400 MHz CSIDs, the full size rear stream, votes MMCX at SVS,
which MX follows, one level short of its PLL.

Take MX as a second power domain at SVS_L1, like the newer camera clock
controllers. 1520 MHz only runs for a 760 MHz IFE, whose MMCX vote at
NOM MX follows. The probe resumed the device and configured the PLLs
before a second domain could be attached; let the common probe do it in
order, with the PLL configurations in the descriptor.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
